#, no-wrap
msgid "Import the packages and define two helpers: one that trains a random forest, and one that computes the metrics used throughout the tutorial.\n"
msgstr "Impor paket-paketnya dan definisikan dua fungsi bantu: satu untuk melatih random forest, dan satu lagi untuk menghitung metrik yang dipakai di sepanjang tutorial ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure IBM Quantum credentials {#configure-ibm-quantum-credentials}"
msgstr "Konfigurasi kredensial IBM Quantum {#configure-ibm-quantum-credentials}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authenticate with your [IBM Quantum Platform API key](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/), load the Rimay function, and select the least busy quantum processor available to your instance.\n"
msgstr "Lakukan autentikasi dengan [IBM Quantum Platform API key](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/) kamu, muat fungsi Rimay, lalu pilih prosesor kuantum paling sepi antrean yang tersedia untuk instance kamu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay maps every numerical input feature onto one qubit, so the first step is to turn the raw table into numerical features.\n"
msgstr "Rimay memetakan setiap fitur input numerik ke satu qubit, jadi langkah pertama adalah mengubah tabel mentah menjadi fitur numerik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the dataset {#load-the-dataset}"
msgstr "Muat dataset {#load-the-dataset}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the German credit dataset directly from OpenML. The `class` column holds the label: `good` for applicants who repaid their credit and `bad` for those who did not.\n"
msgstr "Muat dataset German credit langsung dari OpenML. Kolom `class` berisi label: `good` untuk pemohon yang melunasi kreditnya dan `bad` untuk yang tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encode the features {#encode-the-features}"
msgstr "Encode fitur {#encode-the-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert the label to a binary value, and one-hot encode the 13 categorical columns. The code drops the first category of each column to avoid redundant features, which results in 48 numerical features.\n"
msgstr "Ubah label menjadi nilai biner, dan lakukan one-hot encoding pada 13 kolom kategorikal. Kodenya membuang kategori pertama dari tiap kolom untuk menghindari fitur yang redundan, sehingga menghasilkan 48 fitur numerik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split into training and test sets {#split-into-training-and-test-sets}"
msgstr "Pisahkan menjadi set pelatihan dan set uji {#split-into-training-and-test-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hold back 20% of the applicants as a test set. A stratified split keeps the share of good and bad credits equal in both sets.\n"
msgstr "Sisihkan 20% pemohon sebagai set uji. Pemisahan bertingkat (stratified) menjaga proporsi kredit baik dan buruk tetap sama di kedua set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Establish a classical baseline {#establish-a-classical-baseline}"
msgstr "Buat baseline klasik {#establish-a-classical-baseline}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train a random forest on the classical features. In Step 4, you compare the quantum-transformed features against its metrics.\n"
msgstr "Latih random forest pada fitur klasik. Di Langkah 4, kamu akan membandingkan fitur hasil transformasi kuantum dengan metriknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the data to Rimay {#upload-the-data-to-rimay}"
msgstr "Unggah data ke Rimay {#upload-the-data-to-rimay}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay reads its inputs from CSV files that you upload to the function. The features and the labels go into separate files. You also upload the test set, so that Rimay maps it with the same mapping it fits on the training set.\n"
msgstr "Rimay membaca inputnya dari file CSV yang kamu unggah ke fungsi tersebut. Fitur dan label disimpan di file terpisah. Kamu juga mengunggah set uji, supaya Rimay memetakannya dengan pemetaan yang sama dengan yang di-fit pada set pelatihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi di hardware kuantum {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay builds and transpiles the circuits for the processor you select, so there is no circuit to optimize by hand. Specify the number of shots per circuit, within the following constraints:\n"
msgstr "Rimay membangun dan men-transpile circuit untuk prosesor yang kamu pilih, jadi tidak ada circuit yang perlu dioptimalkan secara manual. Tentukan jumlah shot per circuit, dengan batasan berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every feature needs one qubit, so the processor must have at least as many qubits as the dataset has features.\n"
msgstr "Setiap fitur butuh satu qubit, jadi prosesor harus punya qubit paling tidak sebanyak jumlah fitur dalam dataset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay runs one circuit per row, training and test rows together. A single job can request at most 10 million executions, so the number of rows times `shots` must stay within that budget.\n"
msgstr "Rimay menjalankan satu circuit per baris, baris pelatihan dan uji digabung. Satu job dapat meminta paling banyak 10 juta eksekusi, jadi jumlah baris dikali `shots` harus tetap dalam batas tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check both limits before you submit the job.\n"
msgstr "Periksa kedua batas ini sebelum kamu mengirim job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"A job must also finish within 24 hours, including the time its circuits wait in the queue, or it is stopped without a result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sebuah job juga harus selesai dalam 24 jam, termasuk waktu circuit-nya menunggu di antrean, atau job itu dihentikan tanpa hasil.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the function size {#calculate-the-function-size}"
msgstr "Hitung ukuran fungsi {#calculate-the-function-size}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job runs at a function size, `S`, `M`, or `L`, which selects the compute resources it runs on. For Rimay, the size depends on the number of rows that a job maps, training and test rows together. If you request a size that is too small, the job fails with error `4600`. For the sizes and their limits, see [Function sizes](/guides/kipu-rimay#function-sizes) in the Rimay guide.\n"
msgstr "Setiap job berjalan pada ukuran fungsi tertentu, `S`, `M`, atau `L`, yang menentukan sumber daya komputasi yang dipakai. Untuk Rimay, ukurannya bergantung pada jumlah baris yang dipetakan sebuah job, baris pelatihan dan uji digabung. Jika kamu meminta ukuran yang terlalu kecil, job akan gagal dengan error `4600`. Untuk ukuran beserta batasnya, lihat [Function sizes](/guides/kipu-rimay#function-sizes) di panduan Rimay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cell defines the size calculator. It runs on your machine, reads only the data that you pass to it, and submits nothing.\n"
msgstr "Sel berikut mendefinisikan kalkulator ukuran. Kalkulator ini berjalan di mesinmu, hanya membaca data yang kamu berikan, dan tidak mengirim apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the data sets in the same order as the files in `input_file`, together with the mode of the run:\n"
msgstr "Berikan set data dengan urutan yang sama seperti file di `input_file`, beserta mode jalannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run Rimay in `fit-transform` mode. It fits a quantum feature mapping on `x_train.csv` and `y_train.csv`, and maps both the training and the test sets with it. The order of the files in `input_file` matters. List the training features, the training labels, and then the optional test features. Pass the size that you calculated as `function_size`.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan Rimay dalam mode `fit-transform`. Rimay mem-fit pemetaan fitur kuantum pada `x_train.csv` dan `y_train.csv`, lalu memetakan set pelatihan maupun set uji dengannya. Urutan file di `input_file` itu penting. Urutkan fitur pelatihan, label pelatihan, lalu fitur uji (opsional). Berikan ukuran yang tadi kamu hitung sebagai `function_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monitor the job {#monitor-the-job}"
msgstr "Pantau job {#monitor-the-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status of the job while it runs. `job.result()` blocks until the job has finished.\n"
msgstr "Periksa status job selagi berjalan. `job.result()` akan menunggu sampai job selesai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result holds a `mapping_id`, which identifies the mapping that this run fitted. You do not need it in this tutorial, because the test set was mapped in the same run. Record this ID if you want to map new rows later with `mode=\"transform\"`. It is the only way to access the fitted mapping, and without it, you must fit and pay for a new one. The mapping is built for the qubit layout of this processor, so a later `transform` run must pass the same `backend_name`.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya berisi `mapping_id`, yang mengidentifikasi pemetaan yang di-fit oleh run ini. Kamu tidak membutuhkannya di tutorial ini, karena set uji sudah dipetakan dalam run yang sama. Simpan ID ini kalau kamu ingin memetakan baris baru nanti dengan `mode=\"transform\"`. Ini satu-satunya cara untuk mengakses pemetaan yang sudah di-fit, dan tanpanya, kamu harus melakukan fit lagi dan membayar untuk pemetaan baru. Pemetaan ini dibangun untuk tata letak qubit prosesor ini, jadi run `transform` berikutnya harus memakai `backend_name` yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return the result in the desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-the-result-in-the-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-the-result-in-the-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the quantum-transformed features {#download-the-quantum-transformed-features}"
msgstr "Unduh fitur hasil transformasi kuantum {#download-the-quantum-transformed-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the files that the job wrote, by using the names in `output_files`. Each name starts with the job ID, so the files of this run stay available after later runs. Pass `target_name` so that each file is saved under its own name.\n"
msgstr "Unduh file yang ditulis oleh job, dengan memakai nama di `output_files`. Setiap nama diawali dengan ID job, sehingga file dari run ini tetap tersedia setelah run berikutnya. Berikan `target_name` supaya tiap file disimpan dengan namanya sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train on the quantum-transformed features {#train-on-the-quantum-transformed-features}"
msgstr "Latih pada fitur hasil transformasi kuantum {#train-on-the-quantum-transformed-features}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train a random forest on the quantum-transformed features alone.\n"
msgstr "Latih random forest hanya pada fitur hasil transformasi kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Train on classical and quantum features combined {#train-on-classical-and-quantum-features-combined}"
msgstr "Latih pada gabungan fitur klasik dan kuantum {#train-on-classical-and-quantum-features-combined}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stack the original and the quantum-transformed features, and train the same model on the combination.\n"
msgstr "Gabungkan fitur asli dan fitur hasil transformasi kuantum, lalu latih model yang sama pada gabungan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the results {#compare-the-results}"
msgstr "Bandingkan hasilnya {#compare-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the three models on the test set.\n"
msgstr "Bandingkan ketiga model pada set uji.\n"

